Description:
    Generates a reactive CRUD resource the way `rails g scaffold` generates a
    plain one: the model and its migration and route come from Rails itself,
    and the controller half is replaced with a hibiki island — a collection
    channel, a per-record channel, a shared query object, a ReactiveForm, and
    views wired through Hibiki::Rails::Helpers.

    Everything is derived from the field list you pass, exactly as Rails'
    scaffold derives its own output. Stock `rails g scaffold` is untouched.

    The generated index is live: search, filter, sort, and pagination are all
    reactive, edits happen in place, and changes from anywhere update every open
    list.

Example:
    bin/rails generate hibiki:rails:scaffold Book title:string author:references

    This will create:
        db/migrate/XXXXXXXXXXXX_create_books.rb
        app/models/book.rb
        app/models/book_query.rb
        app/models/book_row.rb
        app/channels/books_channel.rb
        app/channels/book_channel.rb
        app/forms/book_form.rb
        app/controllers/books_controller.rb
        app/views/books/*
        app/assets/stylesheets/hibiki_busy.css
    And add to config/routes.rb:
        resources :books

    Restart the server afterwards if it is running — app/forms is new.

    Pass --phlex to emit Phlex components under app/views/books/*.rb instead of
    ERB templates. The view layer is the only thing it changes; it needs the
    phlex-rails gem and `bin/rails g phlex:install`.
